        "NC_GLOBAL": {
          "cdm_data_type": "Station",
          "featureType": "timeSeries",
          "station_name": "EOP-Derived-Winds",
          "title": "FRF End of Pier Derived Winds",
          "summary": "Wind data Collected at the USACE Coatal Hydraulics Laboratory (CHL), Field Research Facility (FRF) in Duck, NC. These data were collected on the end of the FRF pier (EOP) with RM Young (RMY) serial output Marine Anemometers with a serial (digital) output. These data are termed Derived since they use a combination of gauges to best estimate the winds.  There is a preferential order to choose a gauge, if the data  record is QC flagged the other gauges are considered.   Data were sampled at 1 Hz and statistics are computed at 10 minute intervals:\n  speed   = 10-min average speed, m/s\n  vspeed  = vector average speed, m/s\n  sust    = highest 1 min average speed, m/s\n  gust    = highest 5 s average speed, m/s\n  minSp   = lowest instantaneous speed, m/s\n  maxSp   = highest instantaneous speed, m/s\n  spdStd  = standard deviation of speed, m/s\n  vdir    = vector averaged direction, coming from, clockwise from true north, deg\n  elev    = gauge elevation (m) from NAVD88 (changes depending on the gauge used)\n  gaugeUsed = integer mapped to the following gauges:\n          ID  Latitude    Longitude  Elev   Description\n    1 =  932  36.183683 -75.745116 18.84  EOP SE boom\n    2 =  832  36.183688 -75.745143 18.84  EOP NW boom\n    3 =  532  36.183678 -75.745137 19.58  EOP tower, RMY Sonic\n    4 =  732  36.183638 -75.745460 19.58  EOP NDBC tower\n    5 =  632  36.182075 -75.751244 19.95  Roof om main building (out of service 1993)\n",
          "history": "USACE/FRF",
          "source": "In situ observations from FRF-met_wind_windDerived_YYYYMM.mat",
          "sourceUrl": "(local files)",
